---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Services" description="Research, pilot design, evaluation and advisory support from Visio Nova Mundi CIC.">
  <section class="hero services-hero">
    <div class="services-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">Work with Visio Nova Mundi</p>
      <h1>Practical support for organisations working on difficult problems.</h1>
      <p class="lead">We help public, community and research organisations understand a challenge, design a responsible response and build evidence for the next decision.</p>
      <div class="actions"><a class="btn primary" href="/contact">Discuss your needs</a><a class="btn" href="/work">Read our approach</a></div>
    </div>

    <div class="unity-world-panel">
      <div class="unity-world-topline"><span>Unity House / pilot architecture</span><span>Cutaway study 01</span></div>
      <div class="unity-world vnm-glass-card" data-unity-world role="img" aria-label="Interactive architectural cutaway of a proposed Unity House community venue showing a hosted kitchen, play and learn hub, welcome portico, people, children and an electric surplus logistics van">
        <canvas class="unity-canvas" data-unity-canvas aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
        <div class="unity-fallback" aria-hidden="true">Unity House · architectural pilot study</div>
      </div>
      <p class="unity-world-note"><span class="unity-note-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>Architectural concept study — not a current operating centre or service.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="sectionHead"><p class="eyebrow">What we can support</p><h2>Four routes into collaboration</h2><p>Each engagement is scoped around the question, the available evidence and the safeguards required. We can begin with a short discovery conversation.</p></div>
    <div class="cards">
      <article class="card"><h3>Research & evaluation</h3><p>Understand needs, service performance and operational bottlenecks, then turn findings into clear recommendations.</p><ul><li>Needs assessments</li><li>Baseline and KPI design</li><li>Process and service evaluation</li></ul></article>
      <article class="card"><h3>Pilot design</h3><p>Shape a controlled, testable response before committing to a larger programme or investment.</p><ul><li>Feasibility studies</li><li>Partner and readiness mapping</li><li>Pilot scope and learning questions</li></ul></article>
      <article class="card"><h3>Impact measurement</h3><p>Build a proportionate way to record activity, learn what changed and report responsibly.</p><ul><li>Outcome frameworks</li><li>Data-quality and evidence plans</li><li>Evaluation and learning reports</li></ul></article>
      <article class="card"><h3>Advisory & capacity building</h3><p>Support teams to improve governance, coordination and implementation while building their own internal capability.</p><ul><li>Workshops and facilitation</li><li>Operating-model reviews</li><li>Implementation support</li></ul></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section callout"><h2>Who we work with</h2><p>Councils, public bodies, universities, charities, community organisations and mission-led partners exploring a measurable improvement.</p><p class="note">We do not present proposed programmes as operating services. Any pilot or delivery work depends on appropriate partners, governance, funding, safeguards and evidence.</p><a class="btn primary" href="/contact">Start a written enquiry</a></section>

  <section class="section callout"><h2>Agree a clear scope before work begins</h2><p>A research engagement could produce a findings brief and recommendations; pilot design could produce a feasibility and readiness plan; measurement work could produce an outcome framework; advisory support could produce an action plan and handover session.</p><p>Deliverables, fees or funding, team capacity and timetable are agreed in writing after the initial discussion. A delivery date is confirmed once the scope, evidence access and partner responsibilities are understood.</p><a class="btn" href="/partnership-brief" download="Visio-Nova-Mundi-partnership-brief.html">Download the partnership brief</a> <a class="btn" href="/documents/Visio-Nova-Mundi-CIC-Capabilities-Pilot-Architecture-2026-27.pdf">Download Capabilities &amp; Pilot Architecture 2026/27 (PDF)</a></section>
  <style>
    .hero{max-width:88ch;padding:12px 0 14px}.eyebrow{margin:0 0 9px;color:#0f766e;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.08em;font-size:12px;font-weight:850}h1{margin:0 0 14px;font-size:clamp(40px,6vw,62px);letter-spacing:-.04em;line-height:1.05;color:var(--text)}h2{margin:0 0 10px;color:var(--text);font-size:clamp(25px,3vw,32px);letter-spacing:-.025em}.lead,p{color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75}.lead{margin:0;font-size:19px}.actions{display:flex;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:18px}.btn{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;padding:11px 14px;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:14px;background:white;color:var(--text);font-weight:800;text-decoration:none}.btn.primary{border-color:rgba(37,99,235,.25);background:linear-gradient(135deg,rgba(39,99,235,.10),rgba(16,185,129,.10))}.section{margin-top:34px}.sectionHead p{margin:0;max-width:88ch}.cards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:14px;margin-top:16px}.card{border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:18px;padding:18px;background:rgba(255,255,255,.88);box-shadow:0 6px 24px rgba(0,0,0,.05)}.card h3{margin:0 0 8px;color:var(--text);font-size:18px}.card p{margin:0}.card ul{margin:12px 0 0;padding-left:18px;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.8}.callout{border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:20px;padding:22px;background:linear-gradient(135deg,rgba(37,99,235,.07),rgba(16,185,129,.08))}.callout p{max-width:88ch}.callout .note{font-size:14px}.callout .btn{margin-top:8px}@media(max-width:700px){.cards{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
  </style>

  <style>
    .services-hero {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(360px, .92fr);
      gap: clamp(28px, 5vw, 58px);
      align-items: center;
      max-width: none;
      min-height: 570px;
      padding: clamp(30px, 5vw, 58px);
      border: 1px solid rgba(37,99,235,.2);
      border-radius: 29px;
      background-image:
        radial-gradient(120% 130% at 88% 8%, rgba(214,232,250,.72), transparent 54%),
        radial-gradient(circle at 14% 82%, rgba(16,185,129,.10), transparent 30%);
      background-color: var(--glass);
      box-shadow: 0 20px 60px rgba(80,130,200,.15), inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,.64);
      -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(20px) saturate(130%);
      backdrop-filter: blur(20px) saturate(130%);
    }

    .services-copy { max-width: 620px; }
    .services-hero .eyebrow { color: #476b91; }
    .services-hero h1 { color: var(--text); }
    .services-hero .lead { color: var(--muted); }
    .services-hero .btn { border-color: rgba(37,99,235,.2); background: rgba(255,255,255,.48); color: var(--text); box-shadow: inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,.64); }
    .services-hero .btn.primary { background-image: linear-gradient(135deg,rgba(37,99,235,.12),rgba(16,185,129,.10)); background-color: var(--glass); border-color: rgba(37,99,235,.22); color: var(--text); }

    .unity-world-panel { min-width: 0; }
    .unity-world-topline { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 12px; margin: 0 8px 12px; color: #476b91; font-size: 10px; font-weight: 850; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; }
    .unity-world-topline span:last-child { color: #1d4ed8; }
    .unity-world { position: relative; width: 100%; min-height: 410px; overflow: hidden; border: 1px solid rgba(37,99,235,.2); border-radius: 20px; background-image: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(37,99,235,.12), rgba(16,185,129,.10)); background-color: var(--glass); box-shadow: 0 10px 40px rgba(37,99,235,.12), inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,.64); -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(20px) saturate(130%); backdrop-filter: blur(20px) saturate(130%); }
    .unity-world::before { content: ""; position: absolute; inset: 0; z-index: 0; background: linear-gradient(rgba(37,99,235,.12) 1px, transparent 1px), linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(37,99,235,.12) 1px, transparent 1px); background-size: 32px 32px; opacity: .32; mask-image: linear-gradient(135deg, black, transparent 92%); }
    .unity-world::after { content: ""; position: absolute; inset: auto -12% -28% 16%; height: 58%; background: radial-gradient(ellipse, rgba(16,185,129,.14), transparent 68%); filter: blur(20px); pointer-events: none; }
    .unity-canvas { position: absolute; inset: 0; z-index: 1; display: block; width: 100%; height: 100%; }
    .unity-fallback { position: absolute; inset: 50% auto auto 50%; z-index: 1; padding: 13px 16px; border: 1px solid rgba(37,99,235,.22); border-radius: 8px; background: rgba(255,255,255,.5); color: #1d4ed8; font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Consolas, monospace; font-weight: 750; transform: translate(-50%,-50%); }
    .is-webgl .unity-fallback { display: none; }
    .unity-world-note { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; margin: 13px 4px 0; color: #476b91; font-size: 12px !important; line-height: 1.5 !important; }
    .unity-note-dot { width: 7px; height: 7px; flex: 0 0 7px; border-radius: 50%; background: #3b82f6; box-shadow: 0 0 0 4px rgba(59,130,246,.14); }

    @media (max-width: 900px) {
      .services-hero { grid-template-columns: 1fr; min-height: 0; }
      .services-copy { max-width: 720px; }
      .unity-world-panel { width: min(100%, 620px); margin: 0 auto; }
    }

    @media (max-width: 520px) {
      .services-hero { padding: 28px 19px 32px; border-radius: 22px; }
      .unity-world { min-height: 350px; border-radius: 22px; }
    }
  </style>

  <script>
    import { mountUnityHouseWorld } from "../scripts/unity-house-world";

    mountUnityHouseWorld();
  </script>
</BaseLayout>
